: "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's trip is booked. The flight and hotel are both confirmed, with one charge each and no duplicates.\n\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 was cheaper at $199, but it has a stop.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest New York hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total: $667.** That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What happened with booking:** I tried to book both together with `book_trip`, but the request timed out. When I retried it, the system said it had failed partway through reserving the hotel. Dana's reservations showed the flight had been booked and charged, but the hotel hadn't. Instead of retrying the combined booking and risking a second flight charge, I booked the same hotel on its own. The flight and hotel are therefore two separate reservations rather than one combined trip.", "type": "text"}]}]}